Licensing Posture Summary
Across the paid licence estate, this tenant has provisioned 1 paid seat, and every one of those seats is currently assigned — leaving 0 unassigned. At this scale, the relationship between provisioned and assigned is essentially perfect: there is no detectable slack between what has been purchased and what is held by someone. The score of 54 out of 100 reflects the boundaries of what this scan could verify rather than evidence of a specific problem, since the checks that would reveal deeper utilisation signals — such as activity against assigned seats — were not available for this tenant's scan.

