Upgrade Opportunities
Upgrade opportunity
These checks returned nothing because your tenant does not hold the Microsoft 365 licence tier they read from. That is not a finding about your configuration and it is not a pass — each one is a measurement this assessment could not take, and each is listed with what holding that tier would make visible. Nothing below is scored, and none of it counts against your readiness figure.

identity:risky-users
Requires Microsoft Entra ID P2. Upgrading unlocks the Microsoft Entra ID Protection risky-user list, meaning the accounts Microsoft has itself flagged as compromised or at risk — the Copilot pillar carries no risky-user figure at all today, which is an absence of data rather than a count of zero.

All three of the areas above — identity & privileged access, mail security, compliance & data governance — are covered by Microsoft 365 E7, so it is named here instead of three separate add-ons. Buying it is done by your own administrator in your own Microsoft 365 admin center (admin.microsoft.com → Billing → Purchase products) — we do not resell Microsoft licensing, so this is a pointer, not an offer.

